=======================================================================
PART B — TWO PLANNED TWINS WERE MEASURED UNFALSIFIABLE AND REPLACED
=======================================================================

Both replacements are DEVIATIONS from 164.7-02-PLAN.md Task 2, and neither was
argued into place: each was run first, and the runner's own verdict is quoted.
The plan's rule is "fix at the arm, not at the twin"; here the ARM is the claim
worth keeping and the TWIN was the thing that could not express it, so the fix
is at the twin and the reasoning is recorded in the gate file beside each arm.

--- B1. arm C1, planned twin: rename the VAULT key lookup ---------------
Planned:  find "WHERE name = 'analytics_service_key'"
          replace "WHERE name = 'analytics_service_key_never'"
OBSERVED (run.mjs --file, log .../scratchpad/p02-arms/counterfactual.log):

    arm C1                       exit   3  WRONG-ARM(U1)  (1.1s)
    wrong-first-failure   C1
        first failure was "U1", not "C1" — red-anywhere is not success

WHY: arm U1 runs BEFORE C1 and asks for the URL raise. Renaming the vault key
makes the KEY guard fire for every caller, so U1 sees the key message where it
expected the url message and fails first. Red-anywhere is not success.
REPLACED WITH: the symmetric edit on the SETTINGS lookup —
    find "WHERE s.key = 'analytics_service_url'"
    replace "WHERE s.key = 'analytics_service_url_never'"
which leaves V1 and U1 green (both are ASKING for a raise, and both still get
the one they ask for) and reddens C1 alone. It also survives the migration's own
STEP 3 body check, because "analytics_service_url_never" still contains
"analytics_service_url" — verified by the arm going RED rather than the apply
aborting.

--- B2. arm R3, planned twin: DROP POLICY system_settings_service_all ---
OBSERVED (same run):

    arm R3                       exit   0  NO-RED  (1.0s)
    no-red                R3
        the mutation applied (occurrence count verified) but the gate still
        passed — this arm cannot fail

WHY: `service_role` is created BYPASSRLS — on the pg-lane
(scripts/pg-lane/run.sh: `CREATE ROLE service_role NOLOGIN BYPASSRLS`) and on
Supabase itself. Row-level security is not consulted for that role at all, so
its `*_service_all` policy is belt-and-braces and removing it changes nothing
observable. ⚠️ This is a property of every `*_service_all` policy in this
repository, not of this table; a twin of this shape on any of them would be
equally unfalsifiable.
REPLACED WITH: an over-broadening of the migration's OWN anon hardening —
    find "REVOKE ALL ON TABLE public.system_settings FROM anon;"
    replace "REVOKE ALL ON TABLE public.system_settings FROM anon, service_role;"
which fails at the GRANT layer, before RLS is consulted, and is the realistic
regression: a later hardening pass widening a REVOKE it did not re-read. R1 and
R2 stay green under it (anon is still revoked, authenticated is untouched), so
R3 is the first failure.


