PART C — NEUTER N1: an arm made unable to fail is CAUGHT
=======================================================================
WHAT: arm V1's message-assertion raise head was changed from
      `RAISE EXCEPTION 'TEST FAILED (V1): the callable did raise …` to
      `RAISE NOTICE 'TEST FAILED (V1): the callable did raise …`.
      That is the minimal neuter: the identity text is untouched, only the
      severity changes, so the arm can no longer fail while still PRINTING the
      string the detector reads. It is deliberately the harder case.

BEFORE sha256: e65528c4080a94b503937f8bfb83fefd8cbed1e5e8519af479aa107816abca1b

OBSERVED (node scripts/mutation-runner/run.mjs --file <gate>, exit 1):

    arm V1                       exit   0  SYNTHESISED(V1)  (1.0s)
    biting: 6        (was 7)
    ❌ 1 defect(s):
    KIND                  ARM
    synthesised-identity  V1
        MEASURE_FAIL: the lane emitted TEST FAILED (V1), which this runner's
        gate file did not raise. WHY IT IS NOT ATTRIBUTABLE: severity is NOTICE,
        not ERROR — a NOTICE/WARNING cannot fail an arm. … The mutation
        satisfied the DETECTOR instead of the arm. This arm is NOT counted as
        biting. Mutate the code under test, never the failure output.

DEFECT KIND PRINTED: synthesised-identity (a MEASURE_FAIL), and the biting count
fell 7 -> 6. Both halves matter: the kind names WHY, and the count is what
ARMS_FLOOR bounds, so the same neuter reaching main would trip the ratchet in CI
even if a reader ignored the defect table.

